.TH ERSEC 1 "September 2026" "ERSEC 29.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ersec \- evidence-driven web, API and security-behavior assessment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ersec
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ERSEC 29.1.0 is an authorized, bounded, non-destructive application-security
assessment platform. It correlates application behavior, authorization,
evidence and release assurance without treating missing evidence as a pass.
.SH SAFETY
Active assessment requires operator authorization and scope controls. ERSEC
does not provide credential theft, persistence, destructive exploitation or
automated data extraction workflows.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the ERSEC version.
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run the built-in offline self-test suite.
.TP
.B --capabilities
Print the capability manifest without scanning a target.
.TP
.B --roadmap-audit DIRECTORY
Audit ERSEC 29.1.0 roadmap coverage for a source tree.
.TP
.B --build-assurance DIRECTORY
Run offline source/package reproducibility assurance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
python3 ersec.py --self-test
python3 ersec.py --build-assurance . --build-assurance-out build-assurance-29.1.0.json
python3 ersec.py -t https://authorized.example.test --profile safe-api
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR nuclei (1),
.BR zaproxy (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ERSEC Project
